Perhaps time for a small recap: goal was to gain weight, build strength, not regress on bike and run, and to try to do the necessary minimum in the pool. I've managed to gain weight alright, at 70.4 kg currently.

Race shoes. After lots of research (both for suitability and availability) I ended up getting [Brookes Hyperion 2 Max](https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2024/07/brooks-hyperion-max-2-review-2024.html). The requirements were:

* not so expensive / not so fragile that I will not be able to do enough training miles in them
* some stability
* *not* a stiff ultra-bouncy supershoe (not used to them, rumours have it they increase feet, ankle and hamstring injury risks: precisely what I don't want)
* some little bounce in the foam would be nice
* enough cushion to do longer rides in come May/June
